    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [x] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [x] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n- [x] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version of the `main` branch\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.ai\n\n### Neovim version\n\n0.12 (!at least latest Nightly build!)\n\n### Description\n\nA negative frontier like `%f[^_]` at the beginning of a pattern causes an error.\n\nhttps://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/cad365c212fb1e332cb93fa8f72697125799d00a/lua/mini/ai.lua#L1872\n\nhttps://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/cad365c212fb1e332cb93fa8f72697125799d00a/lua/mini/ai.lua?plain=1#L1467\n\n```sh\nE5108: Lua: (mini.ai) Could not extract proper positions (two or four empty captures) from string 'test' with extraction pattern '%f[^_]%l+'.\nstack traceback:\n        [C]: in function 'error'\n        .../share/nvim/site/pack/core/opt/mini.nvim/lua/mini/ai.lua:2268: in function 'error'\n        .../share/nvim/site/pack/core/opt/mini.nvim/lua/mini/ai.lua:2081: in function 'extract_span'\n        .../share/nvim/site/pack/core/opt/mini.nvim/lua/mini/ai.lua:1555: in function 'extract'\n        .../share/nvim/site/pack/core/opt/mini.nvim/lua/mini/ai.lua:1562: in function 'find_textobject_region'\n        .../share/nvim/site/pack/core/opt/mini.nvim/lua/mini/ai.lua:620: in function 'find_textobject'\n        .../share/nvim/site/pack/core/opt/mini.nvim/lua/mini/ai.lua:1111: in function 'select_textobject'\n        [string \":lua\"]:1: in main chunk\n```\n\n### Reproduction\n\n```lua\nvim.pack.add({ { src = \"https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim\" } })\nrequire(\"mini.ai\").setup({ custom_textobjects = { e = { \"%f[^_]%l+\" } } })\n-- __test\n```\n\n```\n3j0\ndae -- An error\n```",
