        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the issue!\n\nAlthough not ideal, this is kind of expected. In the example, `'%f[^_]%l+` pattern with the whole line as an input matches `test`. But with `test` as input it does not match. It is [more or less documented](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/cad365c212fb1e332cb93fa8f72697125799d00a/doc/mini-ai.txt#L267-L270) that the last pattern should also be able extract from the matched string, but it does not in this case.\n\nThere is a solution hinted [in this example](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/cad365c212fb1e332cb93fa8f72697125799d00a/doc/mini-ai.txt#L350-L358): explicitly add `'^().*()$'` as the last extraction pattern and it works.",
